Independently audit one proposed new memory identity against existing canonical identities of the already-fixed
ontology type. Decide identity only; do not change type, page maturity, containment, or claim ownership.

Return `existing` only when the supplied evidence affirmatively establishes the same continuing real-world subject
through a stable name plus defining history, an explicit alias or rename, or another source-grounded continuity link.
Return `review_required` when an existing identity is materially plausible but the evidence cannot distinguish
sameness from a different subject. Return `distinct` only when the evidence supports a genuinely separate subject or
no existing identity is materially plausible. Do not treat shared vocabulary, type, role, or being the only candidate
as identity evidence. Cite the evidence and exact registry facts used. Return JSON matching the schema.
